From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Sun, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Serve astro://whats-new from Astro, under upstream's own host

The page a browser shows after it updates is the browser's own statement about
itself, so Astro's is Astro's: an entry of the single WebUI app, compiled into
astro_webui_resources.pak, themed by astro_theme.mojom, and declaring
`connect-src 'none'`. Upstream's fetches its content from Google.

WHAT THIS FIXES, WHICH IS MORE THAN A SWAP

The host was not merely upstream's, it was DEAD. `WhatsNewUIConfig` overrides
`IsWebUIEnabled` to return `whats_new::IsEnabled()`, and that function reads

    #if BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
      return true;
    #elif !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
      return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(whats_new::kForceEnabled);

`kForceEnabled` is `FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT`, and Astro builds with
`google_chrome_branding = false`, so the config declined every navigation.
Measured against the binary this tree builds: `chrome://whats-new` answers
net::ERR_INVALID_URL and commits chrome-error://chromewebdata/. Astro shipped a
What's New page nobody could reach, in a directory beside the executable, for
as long as it has had one.

WHY THE REGISTRATION IS SWAPPED AND NOT ADDED

`WebUIConfigMap::AddWebUIConfigImpl` CHECKs on a duplicate origin, so a second
config for `whats-new` crashes the browser at startup rather than shadowing
upstream's. `AstroWhatsNewUIConfig` has existed in the overlay since before
this patch and was never registered anywhere, which is why that crash was
never observed.

Unlike the settings takeover in 060, no extension grant rides on the host:
`grep -n 'chrome://whats-new' chrome/common/extensions/api/_api_features.json
extensions/common/api/_api_features.json` finds nothing. The host is taken
because it is the address the browser's own affordances navigate to, and a
page at a different host would leave those pointing at nothing.

WHAT UPSTREAM'S WHAT'S NEW LOSES

Its registration, and nothing else. `WhatsNewUI`, its handler, its fetcher and
its storage service are still compiled and still linked; the mojom, the
registrar and the surveys machinery are untouched. This patch removes one line
and the include that only that line needed.

Owned by https://github.com/OxyHQ/Astro/issues/14.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_alia_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_ntp_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_settings_ui.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_whats_new_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/about/about_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/accessibility/accessibility_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/actor_internals/actor_internals_ui.h"
@@ -163,7 +164,6 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/browser_switch/browser_switch_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/history_sync_optin/history_sync_optin_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/updater/updater_ui.h"
-#include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/whats_new/whats_new_ui.h"
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || \
@@ -408,7 +408,7 @@ void RegisterChromeWebUIConfigs() {
   map.AddWebUIConfig(std::make_unique<HistorySyncOptinUIConfig>());
   map.AddWebUIConfig(std::make_unique<OnDeviceTranslationInternalsUIConfig>());
   map.AddWebUIConfig(std::make_unique<WebAppSettingsUIConfig>());
-  map.AddWebUIConfig(std::make_unique<WhatsNewUIConfig>());
+  map.AddWebUIConfig(std::make_unique<astro::AstroWhatsNewUIConfig>());
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || \
